meta {
  name: create admin
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/admins/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required. Becomes both the login email and the username. Must be unused.
    "email": "new.manager@vidaverde.test",

    // Required. Display name.
    "name": "New Manager",

    // Required, at least 6 characters. Also stored in clear text on
    // Admin.password_txt so a master admin can look it up later -- see the
    // note in the docs below.
    "password": "vidaverde123",

    // Optional, defaults to "manager". One of: "master", "manager".
    // "master" additionally unlocks these admins/ endpoints.
    "role": "manager"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  **Master admin only.** `GET` lists staff accounts, `POST` creates one.

  `PATCH /administrator/admins/<id>/` edits name, role, active or `password_txt`
  -- sending `password_txt` also resets the real login password, so the two stay
  in step.

  `DELETE /administrator/admins/<id>/` deactivates the account (sets
  `active: false` and `is_active: false`) rather than deleting it, because blog
  posts reference their author. A master cannot deactivate their own account.

  **Security note.** `password_txt` stores a working password in clear text. It
  is modelled that way on purpose (it is on the ERD), but it means any database
  dump or backup leaks live credentials, and it is only ever returned to a master
  admin. Do not surface it anywhere else.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "admin": {
      "id": "1f4b8c02-7d63-4a19-8e50-2c9f7b3d1a86",
      "email": "new.manager@vidaverde.test",
      "name": "New Manager",
      "role": "manager",
      "password_txt": "vidaverde123",
      "active": true,
      "created_at": "2026-09-05T09:12:00.000000-05:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-05T09:12:00.000000-05:00"
    }
  }
}
